        <mxCell id="c109" value="&lt;i&gt;The tab Ex 14.5 with the first of its three queries selected and run, as Tutorial 14.2 runs a part of a tab. The tab has the DEFINE block and the query for fiscal 2026; the next query&#x27;s comment shows below it. Outlined in coral: Customer Rows, 220 in every row, because a selection on Item or Date never reaches the Customer table; in teal: Customers Invoiced and Customer Rows Both, equal in every row. The five counts add up to 765 against 209 customers in the year, because customers buy from several groups. The count on the Update model button is the measures the query defines.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="790" width="860" height="68" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
